+## Operator scope ruling 2026-07-28 (Ruling A — supersedes Goal & Done)
+Measurement (S1/S2, verified across R2–R4) showed the churn premise
+wrong: of ~170 failures per run only a small open-ended pool actually
+flaked, while 154 ids fail deterministically on clean main — real
+drift and regressions, not flake. Ruling A narrows F251 to what its
+title names:
+- Scope = flake stabilization. DONE = the achieved state: three
+  consecutive full-suite runs (pytest -n auto -q) with identical
+  failure sets, 0 churning ids, 0 quarantined tests — every flake
+  closed by a hermetic fix.
+- The 154 standing-red ids (13 classes, catalog:
+  .agent/f251_baseline/class_map.txt) are explicitly OUT of F251's
+  scope. Their paydown is registered item F252 (T1_F252.md), ordered
+  before F050.
+- The two stopped F-A ids (real-Vite port binding, supervisor
+  teardown guard) move to F252, not into F251's closure.
+- F251 proceeds to normal closure on this definition.
